    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Byzantium was founded by colonists from Megara, traditionally in 667 BCE, on the promontory that commands the Bosporus.</li><li>It grew rich from tuna fishing, tolls and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> grain trade, and the great powers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> fought for its loyalty.</li><li>After centuries as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> it lost its freedom under Vespasian; Constantine refounded it as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 330 CE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> tells how the Persian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/megabazus">Megabazus</a> called the people of Chalcedon blind for settling on the Asian shore when the far better site of Byzantium lay opposite.</p></aside>
    </section>

